  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UK funding to the Humanitarian-Development-Peacebuilding Partnership Facility (HDPP)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The PBSO&#x2019;s Partnership Facility supports greater alignment, coherence, and synergies between the UN and International Financial Institutions to advance shared prevention and transition priorities, via advisory support, liaison, and small grants to UN entities. The Facility also regularly supports UN engagement in Risk and Resilience Assessments, FCV envelopes, and other processes.

The Facility includes two funding windows: (1) a &#x201C;Regular Track&#x201D; that grants up to $200,000 (exceptionally $400,000 upon prior agreement) to provide surge support in a strategically significant area where there is an opportunity for innovation or greater impact by delivering alongside IFIs, with a view of institutionalising knowledge / practice, and (2) a &#x201C;Fast Track&#x201D; that grants up to $50,000, or 100 consultancy workdays (extendable once), for the rapid deployment of capacity in other prevention settings to achieve country/regional results via joint analysis or strategic planning.</narrative>
  </description>
